IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `sg-core`
IMPORT `sg-periods`

-- Companies Act 1967 (Singapore), 2020 Revised Edition (SSO informal consolidation, version in force 6/5/2026 to 20/10/2026):
-- Part 5 Division 3, ss 176, 177 and 182 -- convening an extraordinary general meeting on requisition, calling meetings, the Court's power to order a meeting.
-- Layer 1 (the law, objectively). Periods are counted only by sg-periods.l4. Percentages are tested by integer comparison (a share count times 100 against the
-- percentage times the total), never by division, so that an exact 10% or 5% counts as "not less than".
-- The directors' "immediately proceed duly to convene" and "as soon as practicable" are open-textured judgments taken as plain inputs.

§ `Section 176(1) and (1A): the requisition and the directors' duty`

-- (1A): "any of the company's paid-up shares held as treasury shares are to be disregarded".
-- src:15940 | (1A) For the purposes of subsection (1), any of the company’s
-- src:15941 | paid‑up shares held as treasury shares are to be disregarded.
@ref s 176(1A) (src:15940-15941)
GIVEN `the total number of paid-up shares that carry the right of voting at general meetings` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those shares held as treasury shares` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 176(1A) the number of paid-up shares counted` MEANS
    `the total number of paid-up shares that carry the right of voting at general meetings` MINUS `the number of those shares held as treasury shares`

-- (1): "on the requisition of members holding at the date of the deposit of the requisition not less than 10% of the total number of paid-up shares as at the date of the deposit carries the right of
-- voting at general meetings or, in the case of a company not having a share capital, of members representing not less than 10% of the total voting rights of all members having at that date a right to vote".
-- src:15926 | 176.—(1) The directors of a company, despite anything in its
-- src:15927 | constitution, must, on the requisition of members holding at the date
-- src:15928 | of the deposit of the requisition not less than 10% of the total number
-- src:15929 | of paid‑up shares as at the date of the deposit carries the right of
-- src:15930 | voting at general meetings or, in the case of a company not having a
-- src:15931 | share capital, of members representing not less than 10% of the total
-- src:15932 | voting rights of all members having at that date a right to vote at
-- src:15933 | general meetings, immediately proceed duly to convene an
-- src:15934 | extraordinary general meeting of the company to be held as soon
-- src:15935 | as practicable but in any case not later than 2 months after the receipt
-- src:15936 | by the company of the requisition.
@ref s 176(1) (src:15926-15936)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of paid-up shares held by the requisitionists at the date of the deposit that carry the right of voting at general meetings` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of paid-up shares counted as at the date of the deposit, treasury shares disregarded` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists at the date of the deposit` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having at that date a right to vote at general meetings` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1) the requisition is by members holding or representing enough` MEANS
    IF `the company has a share capital`
    THEN (IF `the total number of paid-up shares counted as at the date of the deposit, treasury shares disregarded` GREATER THAN 0
             AND 100 TIMES `the number of paid-up shares held by the requisitionists at the date of the deposit that carry the right of voting at general meetings` AT LEAST 10 TIMES `the total number of paid-up shares counted as at the date of the deposit, treasury shares disregarded`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "on the requisition of members holding ... not less than 10% of the total number of paid-up shares ... carries the right of voting at general meetings" (the condition of the directors' duty, its own question)
    ELSE (IF `the total voting rights of all the members having at that date a right to vote at general meetings` GREATER THAN 0
             AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists at the date of the deposit` AT LEAST 10 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having at that date a right to vote at general meetings`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "in the case of a company not having a share capital, of members representing not less than 10% of the total voting rights of all members having at that date a right to vote at general meetings"

@ref s 176(1) (src:15926-15936)
GIVEN `the requisition is by members holding or representing enough` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is in the form section 176(2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1) the directors must proceed to convene an extraordinary general meeting` MEANS
    IF `the requisition is by members holding or representing enough` AND `the requisition is in the form section 176(2) requires`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The directors of a company, despite anything in its constitution, must, on the requisition of members holding ... not less than 10% ..., immediately proceed duly to convene an extraordinary general meeting" (a duty whose condition is unmet)

-- The duty is met when the directors immediately proceeded duly to convene, the meeting is held as soon as practicable, and it is held not later than 2 months after the company received the requisition.
@ref s 176(1) (src:15926-15936)
GIVEN `the directors immediately proceeded duly to convene the extraordinary general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the meeting is held as soon as practicable` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the company received the requisition` IS A DATE
      `the date the extraordinary general meeting is held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(1) the directors have complied with the duty to convene` MEANS
    IF    `the directors immediately proceeded duly to convene the extraordinary general meeting`
      AND `the meeting is held as soon as practicable`
      AND `the date the extraordinary general meeting is held` AT MOST (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company received the requisition` 2 Months)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "immediately proceed duly to convene an extraordinary general meeting of the company to be held as soon as practicable but in any case not later than 2 months after the receipt by the company of the requisition" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)

GIVEN `the date the company received the requisition` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 176(1) the number of days from receipt to the last day for the meeting` MEANS
    (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date the company received the requisition` 2 Months) MINUS `the date the company received the requisition`

-- src:15945 | (2) The requisition must state the objects of the meeting and must
-- src:15946 | be signed by the requisitionists and deposited at the registered office
-- src:15947 | of the company, and may consist of several documents in like form
-- src:15948 | each signed by one or more requisitionists.
@ref s 176(2) (src:15945-15948)
GIVEN `the requisition states the objects of the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is signed by the requisitionists` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition is deposited at the registered office of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the requisition consists of several documents` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the documents are in like form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `each document is signed by one or more requisitionists` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(2) the requisition is in the form the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF NOT (`the requisition states the objects of the meeting` AND `the requisition is signed by the requisitionists` AND `the requisition is deposited at the registered office of the company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The requisition must state the objects of the meeting and must be signed by the requisitionists and deposited at the registered office of the company" (a duty's own question)
    ELSE (IF `the requisition consists of several documents`
          THEN (IF `the documents are in like form` AND `each document is signed by one or more requisitionists`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE NOTHING)   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "may consist of several documents in like form each signed by one or more requisitionists" -- several documents not in like form, or not each signed, are outside the permission the text gives (F-18)
          ELSE JUST TRUE)

§ `Section 176(3) to (5): the requisitionists may convene; expenses; special resolutions`

-- (3): "If the directors do not within 21 days after the date of the deposit of the requisition proceed to convene a meeting, the requisitionists, or any of them representing more than 50% of the total voting
-- rights of all of them, may themselves, in the same manner as nearly as possible ..., convene a meeting". A grant with an "if" gate: when it fails, NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1; F-19).
-- src:15950 | (3) If the directors do not within 21 days after the date of the deposit
-- src:15951 | of the requisition proceed to convene a meeting, the requisitionists, or
-- src:15952 | any of them representing more than 50% of the total voting rights of
-- src:15953 | all of them, may themselves, in the same manner as nearly as possible
-- src:15954 | as that in which meetings are to be convened by directors convene a
-- src:15955 | meeting, but any meeting so convened must not be held after the
-- src:15956 | expiration of 3 months from that date.
@ref s 176(3) (src:15950-15956)
GIVEN `the date of the deposit of the requisition` IS A DATE
      `the directors proceeded to convene a meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the directors proceeded to convene a meeting` IS A DATE
      `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists who propose to convene the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the requisitionists` IS A NUMBER
      `the requisitionists convene the meeting in the same manner as nearly as possible as that in which meetings are convened by directors` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(3) the requisitionists may themselves convene a meeting` MEANS
    IF    (NOT (`the directors proceeded to convene a meeting` AND `period: the date is not later than the end of a period after` `the date of the deposit of the requisition` `the date the directors proceeded to convene a meeting` 21 Days))
      AND 2 TIMES `the voting rights represented by the requisitionists who propose to convene the meeting` GREATER THAN `the total voting rights of all the requisitionists`
      AND `the requisitionists convene the meeting in the same manner as nearly as possible as that in which meetings are convened by directors`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If the directors do not within 21 days ... proceed to convene a meeting, the requisitionists, or any of them representing more than 50% of the total voting rights of all of them, may themselves, in the same manner as nearly as possible ..., convene a meeting" (F-19)

-- "but any meeting so convened must not be held after the expiration of 3 months from that date": a bar. JUST TRUE means the meeting is barred.
@ref s 176(3) (src:15950-15956)
GIVEN `the date of the deposit of the requisition` IS A DATE
      `the date the meeting so convened is to be held` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(3) the meeting so convened is barred because it would be held after 3 months from the date of the deposit` MEANS
    IF `the date the meeting so convened is to be held` GREATER THAN (`period: the last day of a period after` `the date of the deposit of the requisition` 3 Months)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "any meeting so convened must not be held after the expiration of 3 months from that date" -- the meeting is not held after that day, so the bar does not apply (a bar's own question)

-- src:15958 | (4) Any reasonable expenses incurred by the requisitionists by
-- src:15959 | reason of the failure of the directors to convene a meeting must be
-- src:15960 | paid to the requisitionists by the company, and any sum so paid must
-- src:15961 | be retained by the company out of any sums due or to become due
-- src:15962 | from the company by way of fees or other remuneration in respect of
-- src:15963 | their services to such of the directors as were in default.
@ref s 176(4) (src:15958-15963)
GIVEN `the reasonable expenses incurred by the requisitionists by reason of the failure of the directors to convene a meeting, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 176(4) the sum the company must pay the requisitionists` MEANS
    `the reasonable expenses incurred by the requisitionists by reason of the failure of the directors to convene a meeting, in Singapore dollars`

-- "any sum so paid must be retained by the company out of any sums due or to become due from the company by way of fees or other remuneration ... to such of the directors as were in default".
-- The text does not say how the sum is shared among the directors in default; the function states only how much is retained in all.
@ref s 176(4) (src:15958-15963)
GIVEN `the sum paid to the requisitionists, in Singapore dollars` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 176(4) the sum the company must retain out of sums due to the directors in default` MEANS
    `the sum paid to the requisitionists, in Singapore dollars`

-- src:15965 | (5) A meeting at which a special resolution is to be proposed is
-- src:15966 | deemed not to be duly convened by the directors if they do not give
-- src:15971 | such notice thereof as is required by this Act in the case of special
-- src:15972 | resolutions.
@ref s 176(5) (src:15965-15972)
GIVEN `a special resolution is to be proposed at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the directors have given the notice this Act requires in the case of special resolutions` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 176(5) the meeting is deemed not to be duly convened by the directors` MEANS
    IF `a special resolution is to be proposed at the meeting` AND (NOT `the directors have given the notice this Act requires in the case of special resolutions`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "A meeting at which a special resolution is to be proposed is deemed not to be duly convened by the directors if they do not give such notice thereof as is required by this Act in the case of special resolutions" (an "if" gate failed; marginal reading (a), F-15)

§ `Section 177: calling meetings`

-- (1): "Two or more members holding not less than 10% of the total number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury shares) or, if the company has not a share capital, not less than 5% in number of the
-- members of the company or such lesser number as is provided by the constitution may call a meeting of the company." "Such lesser number" is read as qualifying the no-share-capital limb only (F-20).
-- A grant limited by its own threshold: when not met, NOTHING (the grant ruling, limit 1; F-20).
-- src:15976 | 177.—(1) Two or more members holding not less than 10% of the
-- src:15977 | total number of issued shares of the company (excluding treasury
-- src:15978 | shares) or, if the company has not a share capital, not less than 5% in
-- src:15979 | number of the members of the company or such lesser number as is
-- src:15980 | provided by the constitution may call a meeting of the company.
@ref s 177(1) (src:15976-15980)
GIVEN `the company has a share capital` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members who propose to call the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of issued shares, treasury shares excluded, held by those members` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of issued shares of the company, treasury shares excluded` IS A NUMBER
      `the total number of members of the company` IS A NUMBER
      `the lesser number of members the constitution provides` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(1) the members may call a meeting of the company` MEANS
    IF `the number of members who propose to call the meeting` AT LEAST 2
       AND (IF `the company has a share capital`
            THEN 100 TIMES `the number of issued shares, treasury shares excluded, held by those members` AT LEAST 10 TIMES `the total number of issued shares of the company, treasury shares excluded`
            ELSE (100 TIMES `the number of members who propose to call the meeting` AT LEAST 5 TIMES `the total number of members of the company`
                  OR (CONSIDER `the lesser number of members the constitution provides`
                      WHEN JUST lesser THEN `the number of members who propose to call the meeting` AT LEAST lesser
                      WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE)))
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "Two or more members holding not less than 10% of the total number of issued shares ... may call a meeting of the company" (a grant whose threshold is not met; F-20)

-- (2): "A meeting of a company or of a class of members, other than a meeting for the passing of a special resolution, must be called by written notice of not less than 14 days or such longer period as is provided
-- in the constitution." A meeting for a special resolution is outside the subsection (a scope limit with no "only": NOTHING, periods ruling (c)); s 184 governs it.
-- src:15984 | (2) A meeting of a company or of a class of members, other than a
-- src:15985 | meeting for the passing of a special resolution, must be called by
-- src:15986 | written notice of not less than 14 days or such longer period as is
-- src:15987 | provided in the constitution.
@ref s 177(2) (src:15984-15987)
GIVEN `the meeting is for the passing of a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period in days the constitution provides` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
`s 177(2) the number of days of notice the meeting must be called by` MEANS
    IF `the meeting is for the passing of a special resolution`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "other than a meeting for the passing of a special resolution" (a scope limit with no "only"; periods ruling of 2026-11-05, item (c))
    ELSE (CONSIDER `the longer period in days the constitution provides`
          WHEN JUST longer THEN (IF longer GREATER THAN 14 THEN JUST longer ELSE JUST 14)
          WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST 14)

@ref s 177(2) (src:15984-15987)
GIVEN `the meeting is for the passing of a special resolution` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the longer period in days the constitution provides` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
      `the notice is written` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the date the notice is given` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(2) the meeting is called by notice as the subsection requires` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 177(2) the number of days of notice the meeting must be called by` `the meeting is for the passing of a special resolution` `the longer period in days the constitution provides`
    WHEN JUST days THEN
         IF `the notice is written` AND `period: the date is at least a period before` `the date the notice is given` `the date of the meeting` days Days
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "must be called by written notice of not less than 14 days or such longer period as is provided in the constitution" (a duty's own question; a period the text fixes)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): a meeting for the passing of a special resolution is outside subsection (2)

GIVEN `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`s 177(2) the latest day for the notice` MEANS
    `period: the latest day for an act a period before` `the date of the meeting` days Days

-- (3): "A meeting is, even though it is called by notice shorter than is required by subsection (2), deemed to be duly called if it is so agreed -- (a) in the case of a meeting called as the annual general meeting
-- -- by all the members entitled to attend and vote thereat; or (b) in the case of any other meeting -- by a majority in number of the members having a right to attend and vote thereat, being a majority which
-- together holds not less than 95% of the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at that meeting."
-- src:15991 | (3) A meeting is, even though it is called by notice shorter than is
-- src:15992 | required by subsection (2), deemed to be duly called if it is so
-- src:15993 | agreed —
-- src:15995 | (a) in the case of a meeting called as the annual general
-- src:15996 | meeting — by all the members entitled to attend and vote
-- src:15997 | thereat; or
-- src:15999 | (b) in the case of any other meeting — by a majority in number
-- src:16000 | of the members having a right to attend and vote thereat,
-- src:16001 | being a majority which together holds not less than 95% of
-- src:16002 | the total voting rights of all the members having a right to
-- src:16003 | vote at that meeting.
@ref s 177(3) (src:15991-16003)
GIVEN `the meeting is called as the annual general meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice given is shorter than subsection (2) requires` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number of members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the number of those members who agreed that the meeting be called by shorter notice` IS A NUMBER
      `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting` IS A NUMBER
      `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(3) the meeting is deemed to be duly called although called by shorter notice` MEANS
    IF NOT `the notice given is shorter than subsection (2) requires`
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (silent): subsection (3) speaks of a meeting "called by notice shorter than is required by subsection (2)"; a meeting called by notice of full length is outside it
    ELSE (IF `the meeting is called as the annual general meeting`
          THEN (IF `the number of members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting` GREATER THAN 0 AND `the number of those members who agreed that the meeting be called by shorter notice` EQUALS `the number of members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "deemed to be duly called if it is so agreed (a) in the case of a meeting called as the annual general meeting -- by all the members entitled to attend and vote thereat" (an "if" gate failed)
          ELSE (IF 2 TIMES `the number of those members who agreed that the meeting be called by shorter notice` GREATER THAN `the number of members entitled to attend and vote at the meeting`
                   AND 100 TIMES `the voting rights held by the members who agreed` AT LEAST 95 TIMES `the total voting rights of all the members having a right to vote at the meeting`
                THEN JUST TRUE
                ELSE JUST FALSE))   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(b) in the case of any other meeting -- by a majority in number of the members having a right to attend and vote thereat, being a majority which together holds not less than 95% of the total voting rights" (an "if" gate failed)

-- (4): "So far as the constitution does not make other provision in that behalf, notice of every meeting must be served on every member having a right to attend thereat in the manner in which notices are required
-- to be served by the model constitution prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs, if any."
-- src:16005 | (4) So far as the constitution does not make other provision in that
-- src:16006 | behalf, notice of every meeting must be served on every member
-- src:16007 | having a right to attend thereat in the manner in which notices are
-- src:16008 | required to be served by the model constitution prescribed under
-- src:16009 | section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs,
-- src:16010 | if any.
@ref s 177(4) (src:16005-16010)
GIVEN `the constitution makes other provision for the service of notices` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a model constitution is prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was served on every member having a right to attend the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the notice was served in the manner in which the model constitution requires notices to be served` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 177(4) the notice has been served as the subsection requires` MEANS
    IF `the constitution makes other provision for the service of notices` OR (NOT `a model constitution is prescribed under section 36(1) for the type of company to which the company belongs`)
    THEN NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "So far as the constitution does not make other provision in that behalf" and "the model constitution ... for the type of company ..., if any" -- where the constitution makes other provision, or no model constitution is prescribed, the subsection does not say
    ELSE (IF `the notice was served on every member having a right to attend the meeting` AND `the notice was served in the manner in which the model constitution requires notices to be served`
          THEN JUST TRUE
          ELSE JUST FALSE)   -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "notice of every meeting must be served on every member having a right to attend thereat in the manner in which notices are required to be served by the model constitution" (a duty's own question)

§ `Section 182: the Court may order a meeting`

-- The Court's power, for what it means to a director or a member. "If for any reason it is impracticable ..., the Court may, either of its own motion or on the application of any director or of any member who would be
-- entitled to vote at the meeting or of the personal representative of any such member, order a meeting to be called, held and conducted in such manner as the Court thinks fit". A power with an "if" gate: when it fails, NOTHING (F-21).
-- src:16372 | 182. If for any reason it is impracticable to call a meeting in any
-- src:16373 | manner in which meetings may be called or to conduct the meeting in
-- src:16374 | the manner prescribed by the constitution or this Act, the Court may,
-- src:16375 | either of its own motion or on the application of any director or of any
-- src:16376 | member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting or of the
-- src:16377 | personal representative of any such member, order a meeting to be
-- src:16378 | called, held and conducted in such manner as the Court thinks fit, and
-- src:16379 | may give such ancillary or consequential directions as it thinks
-- src:16380 | expedient, including a direction that one member present in person or
-- src:16381 | by proxy is deemed to constitute a meeting or that the personal
-- src:16382 | representative of any deceased member may exercise all or any of the
-- src:16383 | powers that the deceased member could have exercised if he or she
-- src:16384 | were present at the meeting.
@ref s 182 (src:16372-16384)
GIVEN `it is impracticable to call a meeting in any manner in which meetings may be called` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the constitution or this Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Court acts of its own motion` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a director of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the applicant is the personal representative of a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182 the Court may order a meeting to be called, held and conducted` MEANS
    IF    (`it is impracticable to call a meeting in any manner in which meetings may be called` OR `it is impracticable to conduct the meeting in the manner prescribed by the constitution or this Act`)
      AND (`the Court acts of its own motion` OR `the applicant is a director of the company` OR `the applicant is a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting` OR `the applicant is the personal representative of a member who would be entitled to vote at the meeting`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "If for any reason it is impracticable to call a meeting ... or to conduct the meeting ..., the Court may, either of its own motion or on the application of any director or of any member who would be entitled to vote ..." (a power whose gate failed; F-21)

@ref s 182 (src:16372-16384)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182 the Court may direct that one member present in person or by proxy is deemed to constitute the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "may give such ancillary or consequential directions as it thinks expedient, including a direction that one member present in person or by proxy is deemed to constitute a meeting"

@ref s 182 (src:16372-16384)
GIVEN `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the member is deceased` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 182 the Court may direct that the personal representative of the deceased member may exercise the member's powers at the meeting` MEANS
    IF `the Court has ordered a meeting under section 182` AND `the member is deceased`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING   -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "including ... a direction ... that the personal representative of any deceased member may exercise all or any of the powers that the deceased member could have exercised if he or she were present at the meeting"

§ `Regulative rules: the duties of s 176(1), s 176(4) and s 177(2)`

DECLARE `s 176 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 176(1) hold the extraordinary general meeting`
    `s 176(4) pay the requisitionists their reasonable expenses`
    `s 176(4) retain the sum out of sums due to the directors in default`

-- The clock: time 0 is the day the company received the requisition; the last day is 2 months later (s 176(1) number of days).
-- src:15926 | 176.—(1) The directors of a company, despite anything in its
-- src:15927 | constitution, must, on the requisition of members holding at the date
-- src:15928 | of the deposit of the requisition not less than 10% of the total number
-- src:15929 | of paid‑up shares as at the date of the deposit carries the right of
-- src:15930 | voting at general meetings or, in the case of a company not having a
-- src:15931 | share capital, of members representing not less than 10% of the total
-- src:15932 | voting rights of all members having at that date a right to vote at
-- src:15933 | general meetings, immediately proceed duly to convene an
-- src:15934 | extraordinary general meeting of the company to be held as soon
-- src:15935 | as practicable but in any case not later than 2 months after the receipt
-- src:15936 | by the company of the requisition.
@ref s 176(1) (src:15926-15936)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the date the company received the requisition` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 176 act`
`s 176(1) the directors must hold the extraordinary general meeting` MEANS
    PARTY `Board of directors` `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 176(1) hold the extraordinary general meeting`
    WITHIN (`s 176(1) the number of days from receipt to the last day for the meeting` `the date the company received the requisition`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `Board of directors` `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the extraordinary general meeting was not held within 2 months after the receipt by the company of the requisition"

-- s 176(4): the company must pay the requisitionists, and the sum paid must be retained out of sums due to the directors in default. No time limit and no consequence is stated for either duty.
-- src:15958 | (4) Any reasonable expenses incurred by the requisitionists by
-- src:15959 | reason of the failure of the directors to convene a meeting must be
-- src:15960 | paid to the requisitionists by the company, and any sum so paid must
-- src:15961 | be retained by the company out of any sums due or to become due
-- src:15962 | from the company by way of fees or other remuneration in respect of
-- src:15963 | their services to such of the directors as were in default.
@ref s 176(4) (src:15958-15963)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 176 act`
`s 176(4) the company must pay the requisitionists and retain the sum` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 176(4) pay the requisitionists their reasonable expenses`
    HENCE (PARTY Company `the name of the company`
           MUST `s 176(4) retain the sum out of sums due to the directors in default`
           HENCE FULFILLED)
           -- no LEST: s 176(4) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)
    -- no LEST: s 176(4) gives this duty no deadline in days (assumed, not ruled; see notes/lest-without-deadline.md)

DECLARE `s 177 act` IS ONE OF
    `s 177(2) call the meeting by written notice of the length the subsection requires`

-- The clock: time 0 is the day the company starts (the rule is entered); the last day for the notice is given in days from it.
-- src:15984 | (2) A meeting of a company or of a class of members, other than a
-- src:15985 | meeting for the passing of a special resolution, must be called by
-- src:15986 | written notice of not less than 14 days or such longer period as is
-- src:15987 | provided in the constitution.
@ref s 177(2) (src:15984-15987)
GIVEN `the name of the company` IS A STRING
      `the day the clock starts` IS A DATE
      `the date of the meeting` IS A DATE
      days IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 177 act`
`s 177(2) the company must call the meeting by notice of the length the subsection requires` MEANS
    PARTY Company `the name of the company`
    MUST `s 177(2) call the meeting by written notice of the length the subsection requires`
    WITHIN (`s 177(2) the latest day for the notice` `the date of the meeting` days MINUS `the day the clock starts`)
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company `the name of the company` BECAUSE "the company did not give written notice of the meeting not less than the number of days subsection (2) requires before the meeting"
